# Configuration for the Playwright suite ONLY. Committed on purpose: every
# value here is either one of Cloudflare's publicly documented test keys or a
# deliberate dud, so there is nothing to leak and a clean checkout can run the
# tests without hunting for credentials.
#
# This file exists because `.env` stopped being safe to test against. Once real
# Turnstile and Resend keys were added to `.env` for the deployment, copying it
# into the local Worker would have meant:
#
#   - the real Turnstile secret rejecting `XXXX.DUMMY.TOKEN.XXXX`, so the
#     "valid submission reaches the send" test would 403 at the bot check and
#     never exercise the rest of the pipeline, and
#   - the JavaScript-off form post, which skips Turnstile by design, reaching
#     Resend with a live key and sending a real email on every single run.
#
# tests/global-setup.ts reads this file and refuses to fall back to `.env`.

# --- Turnstile --------------------------------------------------------------
# Cloudflare's documented always-passes pair. The secret verifies any token,
# which is what makes `XXXX.DUMMY.TOKEN.XXXX` a valid token in the endpoint
# specs. The site key is unused by the suite — the browser specs stub
# challenges.cloudflare.com and inject the botToken field themselves.
PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=1x00000000000000000000AA
TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=1x0000000000000000000000000000000AA

# --- Resend -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Present but invalid, and that is the point. Empty would trip missingConfig()
# and answer 503 before the pipeline ran; a working key would send mail. A dud
# key means Resend answers 401 and the endpoint answers 502, which is the pass
# condition for "every gate admitted this and only the send refused".
RESEND_API_KEY=re_not_a_real_key_tests_expect_502

# Never a real inbox, and never the practice's (PRD §4). Nothing is ever
# delivered to these — the send fails before it leaves the Worker.
ENQUIRY_TO_EMAIL=tests@example.com
ENQUIRY_FROM_EMAIL=Coventry Dental Concept Tests <tests@example.com>

# --- Rate limit -------------------------------------------------------------
# Fixed rather than random so a hashed key is reproducible across runs while
# debugging. It salts a hash of 127.0.0.1 and guards nothing.
ENQUIRY_IP_SALT=playwright-fixed-salt-not-a-secret
